# admin-ui Styling & UX

Admin dashboard uses **Angular Material 3** for components and **Tailwind CSS** for layout and styling. Do not introduce a second component library for admin screens.

Theme is defined in `src/styles.scss` with `mat.theme()` (dark-only). Palettes live in `src/_theme-colors.scss`. Do not use M2 APIs (`mat.m2-define-palette`, `mat.all-component-themes`, `mat-raised-button`).

## Material 3 component APIs

- Prominent actions: `matButton="filled"` (`color="primary"` | `"accent"` | `"warn"`).
- Text actions: `matButton`.
- Icon-only: `matIconButton`.
- Mini FAB: `matMiniFab`.
- Form fields: default fill appearance — do not set `appearance="outline"` globally.

## List pages (`BaseListComponent`)

- `MatTable` + `MatPaginator` + `MatSort` for data grids.
- Filter form: `ReactiveFormsModule` + `MatFormField` / `MatInput` / `MatSelect`.
- Responsive columns: set `defaultColumns` and `mobileColumns` in `setColumns()`.
- Loading: `SpinnerComponent` from `core/components/spinner/`.
- Row actions: `matIconButton` + `MatIcon` + `routerLink` to detail/edit routes.

## Edit pages (`BaseEditComponent`)

- Reactive form built in `buildForm()`; load entity in `load(id)`.
- Validation errors: `ValidationErrorComponent` from `core/components/validation-error/`.
- Section layout: `app-card`, `app-text`, `app-section-divider` — see `.cursor/rules/frontend/admin-ui-core-components.mdc`.

## Feedback

- Success/error: `MatSnackBar` — use `extractErrorMessage(error)` for API failures.
- Confirm destructive actions: `MatDialog` or `DialogService` from common-ui.

## Styling — Tailwind first

**Default to Tailwind utility classes in templates.** The project already loads Tailwind 4 in `styles.scss`; use it for layout, spacing, typography, colors, and responsive behavior.

```html
<!-- Good: Tailwind in template -->
<div class="flex justify-between items-center gap-4 pb-4">
  <mat-form-field class="w-full md:w-64">
```

### Prefer Tailwind for

- Flex/grid layout, spacing, sizing, alignment
- Responsive breakpoints (`md:`, `lg:`, …)
- Conditional classes via `[class.xxx]` bindings (see angular-20.mdc)
- Simple one-off visual tweaks on wrappers around Material components

### Use component `.scss` only when necessary

Reach for a co-located `.scss` file **only** when Tailwind cannot solve it cleanly:

- Overriding Material internals via `mat.*-overrides` mixins — not `::ng-deep`
- Global theme tokens in `styles.scss` (`mat.theme()`, `--mat-sys-*`)
- Complex animations, pseudo-elements, or selectors Tailwind does not express well
- Shared custom tokens reused across many components (e.g. `.bg-card` using `--mat-sys-surface-container`)

Use `--mat-sys-*` (surface, surface-container-low, on-surface, outline-variant, error, primary, …) instead of hardcoded hex for colors that should follow the theme. Permanent sidenav edges must use `mat.sidenav-overrides` (`container-divider-color: outline-variant`) — M3 defaults that token to transparent.

If you add `.scss`, keep it minimal and leave a short comment explaining why Tailwind was insufficient. Prefer an empty or omitted `styleUrl` when all styling lives in the template.

### Other rules

- Do not use inline `styles:` in `@Component` — use template classes or `.scss`.
- Use native `[class.active]` bindings — no `ngClass` / `ngStyle` (see angular-20.mdc).
- Register new Font Awesome icons in `AppComponent` FaIconLibrary when adding menu icons.

## Shell

- Side navigation: register features in `layout/side-menu/side-menu.service.ts`.
- Page title from route `data.title`.
